From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MementoRC <MementoRC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR quote-stripping on Windows

On Windows, cmd.exe strips backslash-escaped quotes from the compiler
command line before the compiler sees them.  This means the CMake
generator expression -DCMAKE_CFG_INTDIR="$<CONFIG>" (e.g.
-DCMAKE_CFG_INTDIR="Release") arrives at zig-cxx as
-DCMAKE_CFG_INTDIR=Release with no surrounding quotes, so the
preprocessor receives an unquoted token rather than a string literal.
At llvm-config.cpp:299 the code uses CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR as a string
(CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR[0]), which fails with:

  error: use of undeclared identifier 'Release'

Fix with two complementary changes:
1. CMakeLists.txt: guard add_compile_definitions with if(NOT WIN32) so
   the broken definition is never emitted on Windows.
2. llvm-config.cpp: add a #ifndef CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR fallback that
   defines the macro as "." (matching single-config / Ninja behaviour)
   for any build where the definition was not injected.

---
 llvm/tools/llvm-config/CMakeLists.txt  |  9 ++++++++-
 llvm/tools/llvm-config/llvm-config.cpp |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/llvm/tools/llvm-config/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/llvm/tools/llvm-config/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,7 +80,15 @@
 configure_file(${BUILDVARIABLES_SRCPATH} ${BUILDVARIABLES_OBJPATH} @ONLY)

 # Set build-time environment(s).
-add_compile_definitions(CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR="$<CONFIG>")
+# On Windows (MSVC/MinGW), the cmd.exe command line strips backslash-escaped
+# quotes before the compiler sees them, so -DCMAKE_CFG_INTDIR="Release" arrives
+# as -DCMAKE_CFG_INTDIR=Release (no string literal, just an identifier), causing
+# "use of undeclared identifier 'Release'" at line 299 of llvm-config.cpp.
+# Skip the definition on Windows; the #ifndef fallback in llvm-config.cpp
+# provides "." as a safe default (matches single-config generator behaviour).
+if(NOT WIN32)
+  add_compile_definitions(CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR="$<CONFIG>")
+endif()

 if(LLVM_ENABLE_MODULES)
   target_compile_options(llvm-config PUBLIC
--- a/llvm/tools/llvm-config/llvm-config.cpp
+++ b/llvm/tools/llvm-config/llvm-config.cpp
@@ -32,6 +32,14 @@
 #include <unordered_set>
 #include <vector>

+// On Windows the cmd.exe command line strips backslash-escaped quotes before
+// the compiler sees argv, so -DCMAKE_CFG_INTDIR="Release" arrives without the
+// surrounding quotes and the macro is left undefined.  Provide a safe fallback
+// that matches single-config generator behaviour (e.g. Ninja on Windows).
+#ifndef CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR
+#define CMAKE_CFG_INTDIR "."
+#endif
+
 using namespace llvm;

 // Include the build time variables we can report to the user. This is generated
